#lego-legacy-route 1
# LEGO Chess: second run over the same `--data-root` as routes/save-game.route (#159).
# Finds the saved player profile (profiles\prof1.lcp), skips the New Player form straight to
# "Who's playing?" with Ada highlighted, enters the throne room, starts a Quick Game (leaving
# Black on its default computer setting), opens Options -> Load Game, loads slot 1 ('Game') from
# profiles\1save.lcs, visibly restoring 1. e4 e5 and two-player mode, plays 2. Bf1-c4 to prove the
# loaded position is live, resigns cleanly (showing both sides restored to human on the Quick Game
# screen), and closes cleanly (exited 0).
#
# Replay ONLY over a `--data-root` already populated by routes/save-game.route. On an empty
# `--data-root`, the game lands on the New Player form instead of "Who's playing?".
#
# - Space skips Krisalis' logo (flip 290, up at poll 300) and the intro (flip 300, up at poll 300).
# - With profiles\prof1.lcp present, the game boots straight to "Who's playing?" with Ada listed
#   and highlighted (flip 310).
# - (576,420) clicks the green tick (flip 320, let go at poll 300) to enter the throne room as Ada,
#   loading profiles\prof1.lcp and profiles\1save.lcs.
# - (385,285) clicks the chess board (flips 365..366) to open the Quick Game screen.
# - (590,410) clicks the green tick (flip 380, let go at poll 300) without toggling Black to human,
#   starting a fresh initial Western board (flip 495).
# - (200,60) opens Options (flip 505, let go at poll 300); (360,258) opens Load Game (flip 525, let
#   go at poll 300), showing slot 1 'Game' highlighted (flip 535); (392,194) clicks the green tick
#   (flip 545, let go at poll 300), replaying 1. e4 e5 and restoring two-player mode (flip 580).
# - Plays 2. Bf1-c4 (flips 585..606, visible on the board by flip 750).
# - Escape (flip 760, let go at poll 300) opens "Are you sure you want to resign?", and (360,232)
#   clicks its green tick (flip 775, let go at poll 300), returning to the Quick Game screen with
#   both sides now human (flip 815).
# - Closing the window at flip 825 exits 0 cleanly.
